WEBVTT

00:00:09.237 --> 00:00:11.457
♪ Dun-dun-da? ♪

00:00:14.503 --> 00:00:16.070
UGGA:
What is that?

00:00:16.244 --> 00:00:19.160
I've never seen
anything like it.

00:00:19.334 --> 00:00:21.467
[frantic grunting]

00:00:21.641 --> 00:00:23.034
What is it, Mom?
Make it leave.

00:00:23.208 --> 00:00:25.471
There's something about this.

00:00:27.125 --> 00:00:28.561
I think it's...

00:00:28.735 --> 00:00:30.302
the end of the world.

00:00:30.476 --> 00:00:32.521
Looks like I've seen it all.

00:00:32.695 --> 00:00:34.959
Well, that's it for me.

00:00:35.133 --> 00:00:36.569
I'm glad it's you, Chunky.

00:00:36.743 --> 00:00:38.876
-[Chunky groans]
-GRUG: It's not the end.

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:40.529
-[rumbling]
-[grunts]

00:00:40.703 --> 00:00:42.662
It's just the beginning.

00:00:42.836 --> 00:00:46.405
Welcome to our Tomorrow!

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:48.624
♪ ♪

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:50.931
-Whoa.
-Wow.

00:00:51.105 --> 00:00:52.977
-[chuckling]
-Oh, wow.

00:00:53.151 --> 00:00:55.893
[all gasping]

00:00:56.067 --> 00:00:57.982
Look at all this food.

00:00:58.156 --> 00:00:59.810
Guy, are you seeing this?

00:00:59.984 --> 00:01:01.246
You're the best dad ever.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:03.248
-Let's eat.
-Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:01:03.422 --> 00:01:04.771
One moment, Thunk.

00:01:04.945 --> 00:01:07.034
Before we eat,
I'd like to say a few words.

00:01:07.208 --> 00:01:11.604
Let this flag mark the day
I discovered our home,

00:01:11.778 --> 00:01:15.434
filled with
flowers and butterflies

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:17.088
and a sweet babbling brook.

00:01:17.262 --> 00:01:18.654
Huh?

00:01:18.829 --> 00:01:21.179
Here, right here,
all your needs will be met...

00:01:21.353 --> 00:01:23.485
-I'm hungry.
-In a minute!

00:01:23.659 --> 00:01:24.747
Go now! He's not looking!

00:01:24.922 --> 00:01:27.533
-Whoa, whoa.
-[others moaning]

00:01:27.707 --> 00:01:29.448
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.
Just a minute. Just a minute.

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:30.449
One minute.
No, no, no, no, no, no!

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:31.972
Wait, wait. Just wait.

00:01:32.146 --> 00:01:34.235
This is our home, a place
we'll always be together

00:01:34.409 --> 00:01:36.934
forever and ever,
and-and you're welcome!

00:01:37.935 --> 00:01:40.024
I did this.

00:01:40.198 --> 00:01:41.155
Problem solved.

00:01:41.329 --> 00:01:42.765
[stomach growling]

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:43.854
[whoops]

00:01:44.028 --> 00:01:46.378
-[laughter]
-Food!

00:01:46.552 --> 00:01:48.641
Isn't it strange how this food

00:01:48.815 --> 00:01:51.122
grows in perfectly straight
row... [yells]

00:01:51.296 --> 00:01:53.124
[excited grunting, whooping]

00:01:53.298 --> 00:01:54.995
[whooping]

00:01:55.169 --> 00:01:56.605
[chewing noisily]

00:01:56.779 --> 00:01:58.520
[yells, growls]

00:02:00.044 --> 00:02:01.697
[grunts] Ha!

00:02:01.872 --> 00:02:03.656
[both laugh]

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:05.310
[grunting]

00:02:05.484 --> 00:02:06.659
[grunting and noisy chewing
continue]

00:02:13.318 --> 00:02:14.362
[lapping quietly]

00:02:14.536 --> 00:02:16.408
[laughter, whooping]

00:02:16.582 --> 00:02:18.540
[laughter continues]

00:02:24.807 --> 00:02:26.244
[all groaning]

00:02:26.418 --> 00:02:28.594
I don't feel like
eating anymore.

00:02:28.768 --> 00:02:29.943
Mom, am I sick?

00:02:30.117 --> 00:02:32.728
No, honey. You're full.

00:02:32.903 --> 00:02:34.295
Full feels weird.

00:02:34.469 --> 00:02:38.778
[panting]:
I can't eat another bite.

00:02:38.952 --> 00:02:39.779
Wait.

00:02:39.953 --> 00:02:41.955
♪ ♪

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:44.784
Yes, I can.

00:02:44.958 --> 00:02:46.960
Buh-nah-nuh.

00:02:47.134 --> 00:02:48.309
Banana?

00:02:48.483 --> 00:02:52.183
I tasted one once,
long, long ago.

00:02:52.357 --> 00:02:53.488
It was summer.

00:02:53.662 --> 00:02:56.143
The sun was warm
on my shoulders.

00:02:56.317 --> 00:02:58.232
Flowers were in high bloom.

00:02:58.406 --> 00:03:00.234
I was just a cub.

00:03:00.408 --> 00:03:04.108
Well, I ate that banana
in one bite.

00:03:04.282 --> 00:03:06.675
And ever since,
a day hasn't gone by

00:03:06.849 --> 00:03:08.764
without me thinking about it.

00:03:08.939 --> 00:03:10.462
What was it like, Father?

00:03:10.636 --> 00:03:12.072
What was it like?

00:03:12.246 --> 00:03:13.682
No words can describe it, Thunk.

00:03:13.856 --> 00:03:14.988
[inhales deeply]

00:03:15.162 --> 00:03:17.208
No words are good enough.

00:03:17.382 --> 00:03:19.123
-We get it, Dad.
-[grunting]

00:03:19.297 --> 00:03:20.951
Just grab the banana!

00:03:21.908 --> 00:03:22.953
Come here, sweet thing.

00:03:23.127 --> 00:03:25.303
-[animals screaming]
-[gasping]

00:03:25.477 --> 00:03:27.914
[both screaming]

00:03:30.177 --> 00:03:32.745
[all grunting]

00:03:32.919 --> 00:03:34.486
[animals screaming in distance]

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:36.662
[screaming continues]

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:40.971
[all groaning]

00:03:41.145 --> 00:03:42.494
[tapping in distance]

00:03:42.668 --> 00:03:44.583
Do you guys hear that?

00:03:45.976 --> 00:03:46.802
What is that?

00:03:46.977 --> 00:03:48.891
[footsteps tapping]

00:03:49.066 --> 00:03:50.545
[grunts]

00:03:50.719 --> 00:03:51.546
GUY:
What's happening?

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:52.765
I can't see.

00:03:53.809 --> 00:03:54.985
It's getting closer.

00:03:56.203 --> 00:03:57.204
Kill circle?

00:04:00.991 --> 00:04:02.862
Something got over the wall.

00:04:03.036 --> 00:04:04.037
Don't get too close.

00:04:04.211 --> 00:04:06.300
Who knows what kind of weird,

00:04:06.474 --> 00:04:07.823
beyond-the-wall creatures
they are.

00:04:07.998 --> 00:04:10.304
Let's just jab at them
from afar.

00:04:10.478 --> 00:04:11.958
-Jab. J...
-Ow!

00:04:12.132 --> 00:04:14.091
-Jab, jab. [gasps]
-[growling]

00:04:15.005 --> 00:04:16.441
Wait a moment.

00:04:16.615 --> 00:04:19.487
Look past the matted pelts
and gnashing teeth.

00:04:19.661 --> 00:04:23.491
The eyes-- there's
a kind of humanity in them.

00:04:23.665 --> 00:04:25.406
[grunting]:
Ba-na-na.

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:27.452
It's trying to communicate.

00:04:27.626 --> 00:04:30.020
Hope, these are people!

00:04:33.371 --> 00:04:34.807
Cave people.

00:04:34.981 --> 00:04:37.592
I thought cave people
died off years ago.

00:04:41.248 --> 00:04:47.863
[loudly]:
We happy meet you.

00:04:48.038 --> 00:04:50.127
In hearts...

00:04:50.301 --> 00:04:53.608
BOTH:
...much joy.

00:04:53.782 --> 00:04:54.740
Thanks.

00:04:54.914 --> 00:04:57.177
Much joy to you, too.

00:04:57.351 --> 00:04:59.179
Oh. They speak beautifully.

00:04:59.353 --> 00:05:02.313
Oh, forgive our condescension,
friend.

00:05:02.487 --> 00:05:03.357
I'm Phil.

00:05:03.531 --> 00:05:05.707
And I am Hope.

00:05:05.881 --> 00:05:07.405
-And we are the Bettermans.
-The Bettermans.

00:05:07.579 --> 00:05:09.320
"Better man"?

00:05:09.494 --> 00:05:11.757
-Betterman.
-Emphasis on the "better."

00:05:11.931 --> 00:05:14.064
-Well, we're the Croods.
-[Guy groans]

00:05:14.238 --> 00:05:15.152
-And this is...
-BOTH: Guy?

00:05:15.326 --> 00:05:18.024
Wow. Good guess.

00:05:18.198 --> 00:05:19.852
Mr. and Mrs. Betterman?

00:05:20.026 --> 00:05:22.115
-Guy!
-What-What's going on here?

00:05:22.289 --> 00:05:23.769
-Oh, Guy.
-Guy. Guy.

00:05:23.943 --> 00:05:26.032
Hope, it's Guy. Oh!

00:05:26.206 --> 00:05:27.555
Guy, Guy, Guy, Guy, Guy.

00:05:27.729 --> 00:05:29.166
What's going on here?

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:32.169
GUY:
I grew up with Hope and Phil.

00:05:32.343 --> 00:05:34.693
They were my parents'
best friends until...

00:05:34.867 --> 00:05:36.086
HOPE:
Oh, Guy.

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:38.566
We thought we lost
your whole family.

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:40.568
That was the moment we realized,

00:05:40.742 --> 00:05:43.005
in such a dangerous world,

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:45.573
there had to be
a better way to live.

00:05:45.747 --> 00:05:49.055
Wh... [laughs excitedly]

00:05:49.229 --> 00:05:50.187
Is that your home?!

00:05:50.361 --> 00:05:52.624
EEP:
Whoa. That's their home.

00:05:52.798 --> 00:05:54.060
-GRAN: Whoa, mama.
-THUNK: Whoa.

00:05:54.234 --> 00:05:55.453
-Look, Dad.
-Wow.

00:05:55.627 --> 00:05:56.802
[laughing]

00:05:56.976 --> 00:05:58.630
Hey, Guy, race you to the top.

00:05:58.804 --> 00:05:59.935
[grunting]

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:01.676
Oh. Um, excuse me.

00:06:01.850 --> 00:06:03.156
Little tiger girl?

00:06:03.330 --> 00:06:05.550
-Uh, we don't climb this tree.
-Huh?

00:06:05.724 --> 00:06:07.204
There's a "Betterman" way.

00:06:07.378 --> 00:06:08.814
Unofficial motto.

00:06:08.988 --> 00:06:10.294
Ooh.

00:06:10.468 --> 00:06:11.860
Okay, everybody in? Ah!

00:06:12.034 --> 00:06:14.080
-[growling softly]
-Oh. Yeah, the, um...

00:06:14.254 --> 00:06:16.169
death cat will
have to stay outside.

00:06:16.343 --> 00:06:17.649
-See ya, Chunky.
-[Chunky groans]

00:06:17.823 --> 00:06:19.216
[chuckles] Sorry.

00:06:19.390 --> 00:06:23.394
Animals track in
too much, um, dirt.

00:06:23.568 --> 00:06:24.743
Going up.

00:06:24.917 --> 00:06:27.659
GRUG:
Whoa! What's happening?

00:06:29.051 --> 00:06:30.705
Oh.

00:06:30.879 --> 00:06:32.316
[chuckles]

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:34.622
Welcome to the Betterman home.

00:06:34.796 --> 00:06:35.797
-Wow.
-Wow.

00:06:35.971 --> 00:06:37.364
It's beautiful.

00:06:37.538 --> 00:06:39.845
-Kinda big, isn't it?
-[Sandy chomping]

00:06:40.019 --> 00:06:41.499
What? Wow.

00:06:41.673 --> 00:06:42.848
[laughs]:
Whoa.

00:06:43.022 --> 00:06:44.806
I can see the clouds.

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:46.591
But I'm inside.

00:06:46.765 --> 00:06:47.679
What-what is this?

00:06:47.853 --> 00:06:48.767
What is this?!

00:06:48.941 --> 00:06:51.639
Uh, we call that a window.

00:06:52.727 --> 00:06:55.600
[echoing]:
Window.

00:06:55.774 --> 00:06:57.645
-[sighs heavily]
-Okay.

00:06:57.819 --> 00:07:00.692
Uh, Guy, Dawn will be
so happy to see you.

00:07:00.866 --> 00:07:02.128
-Dawn?
-Dawn?

00:07:02.302 --> 00:07:03.738
Yeah, yeah.
We grew up together.

00:07:03.912 --> 00:07:06.393
-Oh, Dawn!
-[Ugga shouts]

00:07:06.567 --> 00:07:08.656
Oh, that's just your reflection.

00:07:08.830 --> 00:07:09.918
It's called a mirror.

00:07:10.092 --> 00:07:11.398
Oh. Sorry.

00:07:11.572 --> 00:07:13.661
-Dawn!
-[Gran shouts, glass shatters]

00:07:13.835 --> 00:07:16.360
-Sorry.
-Dawn!

00:07:16.534 --> 00:07:17.839
Where is she?

00:07:18.013 --> 00:07:19.014
DAWN [muffled]:
I'm in the panic cubby!

00:07:19.189 --> 00:07:20.364
BOTH:
[gasps] Panic cubby.

00:07:20.538 --> 00:07:22.453
Dawn, it wasn't wild animals.

00:07:22.627 --> 00:07:24.063
It's safe to come out.

00:07:24.237 --> 00:07:27.588
[gasping, panting heavily]

00:07:27.762 --> 00:07:29.590
Mom, maybe we should
drill some air holes

00:07:29.764 --> 00:07:31.026
in the door of the panic cubby?

00:07:31.201 --> 00:07:33.203
No air holes.
Snakes could get in.

00:07:33.377 --> 00:07:35.640
But you'll never believe
who we just found.

